Create a pod =>  Kubectl run nginx --image=nginx
Create a  pod via yaml => kubectl create -f pod.defination.yaml
Create a yaml from declerative => kubectl run redis --image=redis123 --dry-run=client -o yaml >tt.yaml
Edit a pod => kubectl edit pod redis
Get properties of yaml => kubectl explain replicaset
Scale a replica set => k scale rs new-replica-set --replicas=2 or k edit rs new-replica-set
Create a deployment and output it into yaml =>  kubectl create deployment --image=nginx nginx --replicas=4 --dry-run=client -o yaml > nginx-deployment.yaml
Get pods from a specific namespace => k get pods -n research
Create a pod in a specific namespace => k run redis --image=redis -n finance
List pods from all namespace => k get pods -A
Create a Service named redis-service of type ClusterIP to expose pod redis on port 6379   => kubectl expose pod redis --port=6379 --target-port=6379 --name=redis-service
(if we dont specifict target port then it will be same as the port mentioned in command)
Create a Service named nginx of type NodePort to expose pod nginx's port 80 on port 30080 on the nodes: kubectl expose pod nginx --type=NodePort --port=80 --name=nginx-service --dry-run=client -o yaml
Replace a pod => k replace --force -f nginx.yaml
